    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13713" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσκλῆναι</span></b> , aor. 2
		inf. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀποσκέλλω</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέλλω</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be
				dried up, wither,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				160
			</span></i>: pf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμῷ ἀπεσκληκέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DMort.</u>
					27.7
				</span></i>
			: and abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέσκλη</span>”
				<i>died of starvation,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Her.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			: fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσκλήσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.37
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.).</div>
